From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leaf Performance experiments <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 07:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the unused goat item sensor

Do not install NEAREST_ITEMS in goat brains. Goat AI never consumes
NEAREST_VISIBLE_WANTED_ITEM, while the sensor otherwise performs item lookup,
sorting, visibility checks, and a memory write every sensing interval.

Source: Lithium 26.1.x ai.useless_sensors.goat_item_sensor, 2No2Name,
revision 701fb2e7636c6d634c76380c11232d27fd578dff.
License: LGPL-3.0-only; independently adapted to current Leaf 26.2.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/animal/goat/Goat.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/animal/goat/Goat.java
index b9f2370..e297c80 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/animal/goat/Goat.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/animal/goat/Goat.java
@@ -69,7 +69,6 @@ public class Goat extends Animal {
         List.of(
             SensorType.NEAREST_LIVING_ENTITIES,
             SensorType.NEAREST_PLAYERS,
-            SensorType.NEAREST_ITEMS,
             SensorType.NEAREST_ADULT,
             SensorType.HURT_BY,
             SensorType.GOAT_TEMPTATIONS
